mode: "100644"
text: "# Hooks & Retention on Reels\n\nWatch-through and sends are the Reels ranking system's top signals — so the hook, the muted-first\nretention design, and the \"who forwards this?\" question are where a Reel is won or lost.\n\n## The first 3 seconds\n\nThe first ~3 seconds decide whether a Reel is pushed to non-followers or throttled. Fire on three\nchannels at once:\n\n- **Verbal hook** — the first words spoken (or the voiceover's). No preamble. On Instagram this\n  doubles as SEO: put the target keyword in the first spoken seconds (see `instagram-seo`).\n- **On-screen text hook** — a bold text line stating the stakes or curiosity. On Reels this is the\n  **primary** channel: most viewers are on mute, so the text hook has to work silently.\n- **Visual hook** — the most striking frame first; motion, a result, a pattern interrupt.\n\nPull the hook mechanism from `hook-writer`. Banned openings: \"Hey guys,\" a logo/intro card, a slow\nestablishing shot, \"In this Reel I'm going to…\". Start *in* the action or the claim.\n\n## Hook angles that work on Reels\n\n- **The bold claim / contrarian** — \"Your most-requested feature is the one to delete.\"\n- **The result / transformation** — show the after first, then earn it (\"this took 14 days\").\n- **The open loop** — \"I lost $40k learning this. Here's the 20-second version.\"\n- **The callout** — \"If you run a SaaS, stop doing this.\"\n- **The relatable / POV** — the shared experience your audience forwards to a friend (\"send this to\n  your cofounder\" energy, without saying it that lazily).\n- **The save-bait tutorial** — \"the exact settings, step by step\" (saves + rewatches).\n\nWhatever the angle, it must be **true** — an over-promising hook with an under-delivering payoff\ncreates a mid-video retention cliff the algorithm punishes, and it burns trust for the next Reel.\n\n## Write the muted version first\n\nDraft the Reel as **on-screen text only** and check it tells the whole story. Then add the spoken\ntrack. If the muted cut doesn't hook and pay off on its own, fix that before polishing the audio.\nBurned-in captions from word one (kept in the safe zone — `instagram-reels-publishing`).\n\n## Retention design — keep them to the end\n\n- **No intro tax.** Value starts at second 0. Cut everything before the hook.\n- **Fast pace.** Tight cuts, no dead air; change the visual every ~2–4 seconds.\n- **Open loops.** Pose the question early, answer it late (\"the third one surprised me\").\n- **Re-hook mid-video** for anything past ~35 seconds.\n- **Front-load value, hold one payoff** for the end to pull completion.\n\n## Design for the rewatch / loop\n\n- **Seamless loop** — end so the last line/frame flows back into the first; it replays without a\n  seam and the viewer watches twice before noticing.\n- **The rewatch trigger** — a fast detail, a dense list, or a \"did you catch it?\" beat that rewards\n  a second watch.\n- **Density** — pack enough that one watch isn't enough to absorb (listicles, settings, steps).\n\n## The sends lever — script for the forward\n\nSends (DM shares) are the dominant discovery signal, and they can be *designed*:\n\n- **Relatable** — \"this is so us\" content people tag a specific friend on.\n- **Useful reference** — the checklist/settings/how-to someone forwards to the person who needs it.\n- **Conversation-starting** — a defensible hot take people send to argue about.\n\nThe test for every script: **who sends this, to whom, and why?** If there's no concrete answer,\nthe idea is reach-capped no matter how good the hook is.\n\n## Retention killers (cut these)\n\n- A slow or branded intro; a logo sting.\n- A hook that only works with sound on.\n- Burying the point; dead air; filler.\n- A hook the Reel doesn't pay off.\n- Ten seconds of content stretched to sixty.\n\n## The measurable check\n\nA good Reels script can answer: what's the **3-second hook** (all three channels)? does the **muted\ncut** carry the story? where's the **open loop**? what's the **loop/rewatch trigger**? **who sends\nit to whom?** If the hook is weak or the sends answer is vague, fix those before anything else.\n"
